            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0562" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11708: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow (Adams) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-08T15:00:00+08:00">January 8, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> reports that the Standard Oil Company’s
                    motor vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Meishan</hi>, under the control of a
                    Chinese <hi rendition="#italic">laodah</hi>, looted today by 20 bandits at
                    mileage 119 above Hankow. The loss was slight excepting that one package of mail
                    and the ship’s papers were taken by the bandits. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Meishan</hi> is now anchored near the <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Oahu.</hi></p>
                <p>Legation informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
